   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must report any thermal incident involving fire, smoke, uncontrolled overheating, injury, or property damage to the relevant regulator within 24 hours of learning of it. Other confirmed thermal incidents must be reported within 5 business days. Reports must include the incident date, product/model, known consequences, and information on units affected; manufacturers must update reports as facts are confirmed. The manufacturer must notify affected customers within 5 business days when an incident presents a credible safety risk to their product or requires a safety action."
