   "final_rule_text": "All new home battery units must support remote emergency shut-off by 24 months after adoption of this standard. Manufacturers must provide a secure means for authorized emergency responders or the system operator to initiate shut-off when necessary to address an imminent safety risk. Existing installed units that do not support remote shut-off are not required to be retrofitted, but manufacturers must disclose that limitation to their owners and provide safe, practical emergency isolation instructions."
